  <section|Status><label|status>

  Draft for independent review. Source pin:
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464> from
  <verbatim|source/upstream.json>.

  Owned prose: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/marked-field-local-estimates.tex>.

  <section|Correspondence><label|correspondence>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Reserve exponent and decay: <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Doors.stain>,
    <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Doors.stain_beats>,
    <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Doors.stain_le>,
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.storms>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.sanded>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/SOURCE_HISTORIES/Delays.lean>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Matter.lean>. <verbatim|Matter.sanded> uses
    <verbatim|wearBeta> for <verbatim|hatBeta_N \<rightarrow\> \<infty\>>,
    <verbatim|Opening.seats \<leq\> \|Index\| hatBeta^k>, and
    <verbatim|temp_cheap> for <verbatim|threshold_N^{-1} \<leq\> hatBeta_N>.
    The prose proves directly the exact tail comparison <verbatim|sqrt(stain
    x) x^(k+1)\<leq\>1> by taking logarithms and comparing <verbatim|exp((log
    log x)^2/5)> with <verbatim|exp(log log x)>.

    <item>Fixed regional mass and cover: <verbatim|YM.Push.RelayDifference.Opening.mitt>,
    <verbatim|YM.Push.RelayDifference.cover_tops>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Straw.lean>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/RELAY_DIFFERENCE/Birth.lean>. <verbatim|regional>
    is the image of the fixed stencil under placement, so its cardinality is
    bounded by the stencil cardinality. The cover uses eventual containment
    in the radius <verbatim|B_N> box, then the <verbatim|Corona.tile> cover
    of the origin halo by at most <verbatim|81> blocks.

    <item>Invitation: <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.inviting>,
    <verbatim|YM.Push.RelayDifference.Opening.presses>,
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.zest>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.platter>,
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.garnish>, <verbatim|YM.Push.RelayDifference.Opening.kickoff>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Parterre.lean>, <verbatim|Champere.lean>,
    <verbatim|Fondue.lean>, <verbatim|Platter.lean>, and
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/RELAY_DIFFERENCE/Opening.lean>. The ordinary proof
    spells out the target coordinate, the healthy-set masking residual, its
    norm price, the exact exponential merge bill, singleton support, density
    reconstruction, forced hook and reserved mass. The terminal marked
    construction supplies the Keeper's canonical support/inventory and
    admissibility dictionary (see Section~\\ref{sec:terminal-marked-construction});
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.garnish> temporarily enlarges eligibility and
    restores the original dictionary through its crossing equivalence. It
    preserves the exact <verbatim|sphere>/<verbatim|Cream> price and the
    source constants <verbatim|81>, <verbatim|4(1+columns)>, and support
    exponent shift <verbatim|+2>.

    <item>Field calibration consumer: <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.solaris> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Canopy.lean>. The other actual consumer is
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.figment> in <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Figment.lean>.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Exact scope and remaining producer><label|exact-scope-and-remaining-producer>

  This unit proves the eventual reserve estimates for each fixed degree and
  stencil, and gives the local marked invitation from a paid section,
  terminal Keeper, read/nonwrapping geometry, and the advertised budget
  inputs. Its inputs are attached later to the selected public run by the
  field calibration consumer. It does not prove the recentering/propagation
  result <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.figment>. That source proof constructs one
  label using <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Relay.antilles> from a
  <verbatim|Cream>, a single selected <verbatim|Music>, its <verbatim|Sung>
  estimates, and all later <verbatim|Tones> and <verbatim|Carol> receipts;
  then <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.toast> adds the selected marked action to the
  backward-dualized Music voice; finally <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.filling>
  transfers the resulting <verbatim|Yeast> estimates to all earlier root
  tests. The finite numerical steps in <verbatim|Figment.figment> use the
  exact choices <verbatim|w=(\<zeta\>_{d,k}/4)/(\|\|alto_k\|\|
  escrow_{N,k}(E))> and the <verbatim|diet> recurrence. Those history and
  height producers remain a separate unfinished proof obligation and are the
  next source target. No implication from local invitation to all-scale root
  tests is claimed.

  The section theorem feeding this result is conditional on a
  gauge-equivariant mark imprint. The actual
  <verbatim|YM.Push.Mark.Linear.unsym> campaign producer is still explicitly
  outstanding in <verbatim|marked-portfolio-calibration-evidence.md>.

